    at Function.invalid (/luxon/src/duration.js:265:23)
    at Function.fromISO (/luxon/src/interval.js:158:30)   <-- unguarded Duration.fromISO(e, opts)
```
Root cause: start parses as a valid DateTime, end is unparsable → the DateTime try/catch works, but then `Duration.fromISO("hello")` is called; `Duration.invalid` throws `InvalidDurationError` when `throwOnInvalid` is set, and that throw escapes. Same for `"hello/2008-05-11T15:30:00"` and `"2007-03-01T13:00:00/foo"` (all → InvalidDurationError). Cases where BOTH sides are invalid (`hello/hello`, `P1Y2M10DT2H30M/hello`, `hello/P1Y2M10DT2H30M`, `foo/bar`, `null`, `""`) correctly throw `InvalidIntervalError`, because they fall through to `Interval.invalid(...)`.
Note: HEAD's code threw `InvalidDateTimeError` for this input, so the edit is an improvement but does not satisfy the stated spec.

### Proof the fix is completable (done in a /tmp copy, repo untouched)
In `/tmp/fixed` (copy of src/test + symlinked node_modules) I additionally wrapped both `Duration.fromISO` calls in try/catch (treat thrown error as invalid duration): `/tmp/verify-fixed.js` → **19 PASS, 0 FAIL**, and `npx jest test/interval` there → `9 suites passed, 127 tests passed`. So the minimal completion is guarding the two `Duration.fromISO` calls and falling through to `Interval.invalid("unparsable", ...)`.

## 4. Final repo state
`cd /luxon && git status --short` (also with `--untracked-files=all`):
```
 M src/impl/util.js
 M src/interval.js
```
I modified nothing in /luxon and created no files there (no `/luxon/tmp-verify.test.js`, no `build/`). Caveat: a **concurrent subagent** was operating in the same container — it briefly created `/luxon/tmp-barrier-check.js` (a DateTime plus/minus script, later removed by it) and it modified `src/impl/util.js` mid-run. My full-suite run before that edit and after it gave identical numbers (2 failed / 892 passed), and my interval results are unaffected by util.js. All my artifacts are under /tmp: `/tmp/verify.js`, `/tmp/verify-fixed.js`, `/tmp/probe.js`, `/tmp/stack.js`, `/tmp/orig/`, `/tmp/fixed/`.

## Bottom line
The try/catch around the DateTime parses is correct and fixes `hello/hello`, `foo/bar`, `null`, `""` (now InvalidIntervalError, previously InvalidDateTimeError), and all valid/throwOnInvalid=false paths pass. But the fix is **incomplete**: `Interval.fromISO("<valid datetime>/<garbage>")` (and the reverse) still leaks `InvalidDurationError` instead of `InvalidIntervalError` because the `Duration.fromISO` calls at src/interval.js:158 and :163 are unguarded. Recommended follow-up: wrap those two calls in try/catch (verified to give 19/19 PASS with no test regressions).

