Now the bug: `DateTime#toISODate() correctly pads negative years`. The existing test at line 57-64 checks year -118040 → "-118040-05-25" (5-digit negative). The hidden test presumably checks e.g. `DateTime.fromObject({year: -100, ...}).toISODate()` → "-0100-05-25"? Hmm.

`toISODate()`:
```js
  toISODate() {
    let format = "yyyy-MM-dd";
    if (this.year > 9999) {
      format = "+" + format;
    }
    return toTechFormat(this, format);
  }
```

For negative years, ISO 8601 requires the sign and 6 digits: e.g. year -100 → "-000100"? Actually ISO 8601 expanded representation: years outside 0000-9999 use a sign and 6 digits (e.g. "-000100"). Hmm, but the existing test expects "-118040-05-25" (6 digits, with sign) for year -118040 — that's the "expanded" form with 6 digits. And "+118040-05-25" for 118040.

